 "notes": "Continuation of Table XV Part II(B) Tri and poly-lingualism. Subsidiary column headers on header pages of this part print 'Dogri.', 'Panjabi.', 'Kashmiri.' (leaf 266 adds letters (B),(C),(D)); recorded as Dogri/Panjabi/Kashmiri. Rows printed nil ('....') in every column are omitted; subsidiary triples all-nil are omitted. Remarks: wrapped lines joined; a word broken across lines ('langu-'/'ages.' or 'langu'/'ages.') is rejoined as 'languages.'. Page 263. Top rows (Pothwari..Shina) complete the Muzaffarabad Tehsil block from leaf 272; printed district label 'Muzaffarabad District.' (Part I name 'Muzaffarabad' in area_path). 'Frontier Districts' is printed here as an italic brace label like a tehsil, placed BEFORE its component units, with no province-level heading; its figures equal the sums of Kargil + Ladakh + Skardu tehsils + Frontier Ilaqas + Gilgit Tehsil (leaves 273-275) for every mother tongue, so it is recorded as the division total (area_is_total true, area_path [State]). In the Frontier Districts block the mother tongue is printed 'Pathwari' (elsewhere 'Pothwari'); kept as printed. Frontier Districts Kashmiri row: Dogri Persons '5' is very faintly printed but legible. Kargil Tehsil block (Ladakh District): Balti/Ladakhi/Shina carry a separate small inner brace but are within the Kargil label. Rows all-nil omitted: Karnah Chabhali, Pothwari, Ladakhi; Frontier Districts Chabhali; Kargil Gojari, Chabhali, Pothwari. Shina remark printed with a space before the full stop ('languages .'), kept."
}